      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "1. Let the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters be x.\n\n2. The value of a nickel is 0.05 dollars, a dime is 0.10 dollars, and a quarter is 0.25 dollars.\n\n3. After accounting for coin changes, we know that 10 dimes are equivalent to 2 quarters, so 5 dimes are equivalent to 1 quarter.\n\n\n\nTip 1 - Calculating Total Value\n\n1. To calculate the total value of the coins, we multiply the value of each coin by the number of coins and add them together like so:\n\nTotal value = 0.05 * x + 0.10x + 0.25x\n\n2. Simplifying this we have:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Total value}&=\n0.05x + 0.10x + 0.25x \\\\\n     &= (0.05 + 0.10 + 0.25) x \\qquad \\text{Add like quantities together} \\\\\n     &=0.40x \n\\end{align*}\n\n3. So we see that the total value of the coins is 0.40x dollars.\n\n4. We are told that the total value is $\\$$13.20 dollars, so we set up the equation:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n0.40x &= 13.20 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\n5. We solve for x by isolating it on one side of the equation. First, we divide both sides by 0.40:\n\n\\begin{align*}\nx &= \\frac{13.20}{0.40} \\\\\nx &= 33\n\\end{align*}\n\n6. So we find that the number of coins is 33, meaning Jamie has 33 nickels, 33 dimes, and 33 quarters.\n\nTip 2 - Check the Answer.\n\nTo check our work, we can use the formula:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Total value} &= \\text{Number of coins with value} + \\text{Number of coins with value} + \\cdots \n\\end{align*}\n\nPlugging in the number of nickels, dimes, and quarters:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n0.40 \\times 33 &= \\frac{33 \\times 0.25}{3} + \\frac{33 \\times 0.10}{3} + \\frac{33 \\times 0.05}{3} \\\\\n&= 0.40 \\times 33 \\\\\n&= 13.20 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\nSo the calculations confirm that our answer is correct. $\\boxed{33}$.",
